# Rule Coverage Validator

## Context

This meta rule exists to ensure all rules in the codebase are:
- Properly configured
- Well-scoped
- Consistently applied
- Effectively documented
- Maintained and updated
- Automatically validated
- Properly integrated

## Rule Configuration Standards

### 1. Rule Metadata
- Every rule must have:
  - Clear description
  - Appropriate globs
  - Correct alwaysApply setting
  - Proper categorization
  - Version information
  - Last updated date
  - Validation status
  - Integration status

### 2. Rule Scope
- Rules should be:
  - Focused on specific concerns
  - Non-overlapping with other rules
  - Clear in their application
  - Easy to understand
  - Practical to implement
  - Automatically enforceable
  - Measurably effective

### 3. Rule Application
- Rules should specify:
  - When they apply
  - How they apply
  - What they enforce
  - How to comply
  - Exceptions if any
  - Validation methods
  - Integration points

## Implementation Guidelines

### 1. Rule Structure
```language
---
description: Clear, concise description of the rule's purpose
globs: 
  - "*.java"
  - "*.ts"
  - "*.js"
alwaysApply: true/false
version: "1.0.0"
lastUpdated: "2024-03-20"
validation: {
  automated: true,
  tools: ["eslint", "sonar"],
  coverage: 95
}
integration: {
  ci: true,
  preCommit: true,
  ide: true
}
---

# Rule Name

## Context
[Rule context and scope]

## Standards
[Rule standards and requirements]

## Implementation
[Implementation guidelines]

## Examples
[Good and bad examples]

## Checklist
[Compliance checklist]

## Validation
[Validation methods and tools]

## Integration
[Integration points and methods]
```

