## Review Checklist

Before submitting a rule, ensure:

1. Rule Configuration
   - [ ] Description is clear and meaningful
   - [ ] Globs are properly specified
   - [ ] alwaysApply is correctly set
   - [ ] Version is specified
   - [ ] Last updated is current
   - [ ] Category is assigned
   - [ ] Dependencies are listed
   - [ ] Scope is defined
   - [ ] Validation is configured
   - [ ] Integration is set up

2. Rule Content
   - [ ] Context is provided
   - [ ] Standards are clear
   - [ ] Examples are included
   - [ ] Checklist is complete
   - [ ] Implementation is detailed
   - [ ] Exceptions are noted
   - [ ] References are included
   - [ ] Best practices are listed
   - [ ] Validation methods are defined
   - [ ] Integration points are specified

3. Rule Quality
   - [ ] No conflicts with other rules
   - [ ] Clear and concise
   - [ ] Easy to understand
   - [ ] Practical to implement
   - [ ] Well-documented
   - [ ] Properly formatted
   - [ ] Consistently structured
   - [ ] Up-to-date
   - [ ] Automatically validatable
   - [ ] Integration ready

4. Rule Maintenance
   - [ ] Regular review scheduled
   - [ ] Update process defined
   - [ ] Version control used
   - [ ] Change log maintained
   - [ ] Feedback mechanism
   - [ ] Review process
   - [ ] Approval workflow
   - [ ] Documentation updated
   - [ ] Validation status tracked
   - [ ] Integration status monitored

